Layer‑1 Smart‑Contracts Engine
CosmaChain — CosmaTech Technologies Inc.
Version: 1.0.0

Overview
The Layer‑1 Smart‑Contracts Engine is the execution layer for all CosmaTech ecosystem logic.
It provides deterministic, modular, Rust‑based smart‑contract execution for:

CosmaCare (health & wellness benefits)

CosmaStar (influencer ranking & visibility)

CosmaGigs (gig‑work payouts & loyalty)

FilmCore (royalties & creator compensation)

CaddiePro (sports scoring & ranking)

CosmaSocial (engagement & creator rewards)

BenefitsAgreement (PTO, retirement, wellness)

RevenueSplit (CosmaTech 12% fee engine)

IdentityBoundTx (identity‑verified transactions)

This layer is fully aligned with the S3E2C3 protocol, the CosmaCoin utility model, and the CosmaTech 1099 Benefits Engine.

Architecture
The Layer‑1 Smart‑Contracts Engine is composed of five major subsystems:

1. Engine Layer
Core execution components:

ABI — encoding/decoding

Contract — contract metadata

ContractState — per‑contract storage

ContractVM — deterministic execution

Dispatcher — routing & registry

2. Types Layer
Shared type system:

ContractEvent

CosmaCoreClient — Layer‑1 Core SDK

Contract type definitions

3. Contracts Layer
Domain‑specific business logic:

CosmaCare

CosmaStar

CosmaGigs

FilmCore

CaddiePro

CosmaSocial

BenefitsAgreement

RevenueSplit

IdentityBoundTx

4. Storage Layer
Persistent contract state:

JSON‑based serialization

Runtime ↔ persistent state conversion

Registry for contract storage

5. Utils Layer
Utility functions:

Crypto hashing

JSON encoding/decoding

Execution Flow
Smart‑contract execution follows a deterministic pipeline:

Layer‑1 Core submits a transaction.

Payload is decoded via ABI.

Dispatcher selects the correct contract.

ContractVM executes the contract logic.

ContractState is updated.

ContractEvent is emitted.

Result is returned to Layer‑1 Core.

State root is anchored to Layer‑0.

This ensures:

deterministic execution

modular contract logic

full S3E2C3 compliance

full CosmaCoin utility integration

S3E2C3 Protocol Integration
The Smart‑Contracts Engine enforces all three layers of the protocol:

S3 — Safe, Secure, Serviceable
Identity verification

Service validation

Fraud prevention

Deterministic execution

E2 — Efficient Economy
RevenueSplit (88/12 engine)

Gig payouts

Royalty assignments

Minimal storage writes

C3 — Cosmic Collective Currency
CosmaCoin utility

Loyalty rewards

Engagement boosts

SCS lifecycle triggers


Domain Contracts
